      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.65,
            0.049,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proportional Reasoning–2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.084,
            0.582,
            0.105
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since it is a direct proportion, we know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.106,
            0.526,
            0.145
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\frac { 5 } { 3 } }   \\times   x   =   1   \\times   1"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.146,
            0.577,
            0.206
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "x = { \\frac { \\frac { 1 \\times 1 } { 5 } } { \\frac { 5 } { 3 } } } = { \\frac { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } { \\frac { 3 } { 3 } } } = { \\frac { 3 } { 5 } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.212,
            0.745,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If they cut the vegetables together, they will finish in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.243,
            0.295,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.268,
            0.847,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Which of the following pairs of quantities are in inverse proportion?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.298,
            0.847,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The number of taps filling a water tank and the time taken to fill it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.341,
            0.847,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The number of painters hired and the days needed to paint a wall of fixed size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.383,
            0.846,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The distance a car can travel and the amount of petrol in the tank."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.425,
            0.845,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The speed of a cyclist and the time taken to cover a fixed route."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.449,
            0.846,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) The length of cloth bought and the price paid at a fixed rate per metre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.491,
            0.846,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) The number of pages in a book and the time required to read it at a fixed reading speed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.533,
            0.775,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. If 24 pencils cost ₹120, how much will 20 such pencils cost?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.563,
            0.802,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A tank on a building has enough water to supply 20 families living there for 6 days. If 10 more families move in there, how long will the water last? What assumptions do you need to make to work out this problem?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.814,
            0.56,
            0.903,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
